# <type>(<scope>): <subject — imperative, lower-case, ≤ 72 chars>
#
# <body — wrap at 100, explain WHY, not WHAT>
#
# <footer — BREAKING CHANGE: ..., Closes #N, Co-authored-by: ...>
#
# --- TYPES ---
# feat      New feature (MINOR bump)
# fix       Bug fix (PATCH bump)
# docs      Documentation only
# style     Formatting, missing semicolons, etc. (no code change)
# refactor  Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
# perf      Performance improvement
# test      Adding or fixing tests
# chore     Tooling, deps, build, non-source changes
# ci        CI/CD workflow changes
# build     Build system or external dependency changes
# revert    Reverts a previous commit
#
# --- SCOPES (enumerated in commitlint.config.cjs) ---
# data, metrics, plotting, analysis, agata, utils,
# docs, ci, deps, release, agents, examples, tests,
# harness, tooling
#
# --- EXAMPLES ---
#
# feat(metrics): add MAGE-2 calculation
#
# MAGE-2 is the second-generation Mean Amplitude of Glycemic Excursions.
# Reference: Service et al., Diabetes Care 2010.
#
# Closes #42
#
# fix(data-loader): handle empty CSV without raising
#
# Empty files were crashing load_from_csv with a generic Pandas error.
# Now we raise GlucoseDataError with a clear, actionable message.
#
# docs(readme): add citation section
#
# --- BODY ---
# Body goes here, separated from the subject by a blank line.
# Wrap at 100 columns. Explain motivation and context, not the diff.
#
# --- FOOTER ---
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description of the change and migration path>
# Closes #123
# Fixes #456
# Co-authored-by: Name <email@example.com>
